+# Compiler retouch — verification summary
+
+Branch `compiler-retouch`, master `2c5d82625` (the current master checkout), which is an ancestor of the branch.
+The delivered compiler source is `7bd374aaf` (merge `9bbf51ce5`), and the delivered commit is the commit tagged
+`compiler-retouch-verified` (`git rev-parse 'compiler-retouch-verified^{commit}'`), which carries this record. Both trees
+are clean-built (`yarn build`, exit 0) from their committed sources and every comparison below uses those builds.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+    yarn workspace @solidcash/utils build
+    yarn workspace solidc build
+    node scripts/verify-id.mjs
+    scripts/gate.sh fast
+    node scripts/metadata-parity-marketplace.mjs <tree> <kernel|framed> <contract>
+    node scripts/body-parity-marketplace.mjs <tree> <kernel|framed> <contract> <resolver-tree>
+    node scripts/profile-marketplace-compile.mjs --kernel --all-declarations --contract MarketplaceV1
+
+## Results
+
+| Check | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Gate identity (both trees) | `{"routeBytes":44865,"fullBytes":246609,"fullHash":"30c4f5a157f93e83"}` |
+| Metadata and `stateLayout` | identical for both contracts in both modes |
+| Full-bytecode hashes | identical for both contracts in both modes |
+| Resolved bodies | identical (full scripts are byte-identical) |
+| Direct medians (three paired runs) | 14,604 → 12,782 ms (87.5%) |
+| `codegen:probe` | 0 ms vs master's 1,610 ms (absent) |
+| Framed medians | 23,151 → 5,736 ms (24.8%) |
+| Framed discarded work | 0 `compileOnce:throw`, 0 `singlePass:verifier` |
+| Artifact JSON | kernel −20.6% / −24.7%; framed −12.0% / −14.5% |
+| Caches | imported parses 24/24, legacy usage plans 16/16, artifacts bounded; all zero after `clearCompileCache()` |
+| Lint | exit 0 |
+| Diff | 39 paths: compiler, SDK, utils, scripts, tests, `docs/` (the kernel-diagnostics note and this workstream record), and the four committed `examples/testing-suite/artifacts/*` fixtures regenerated for compact bodies; no `.marketplace` sources, bench configs or emitted sidecars |
+
+## Body-once direct path (replaces the usage-probe walk)
+
+The direct convention no longer runs a separate usage traversal. For a contract whose dispatch shape is
+multi-entry, `visitContract` compiles every body once with captured helpers inlined and each helper site records
+its span; the contract's own tallies decide the profitable helpers, their DEFINEs are emitted first, rehoming is
+replayed over the recorded ids, and each body is compiled again in the finish phase against the settled defines
+before it is emitted. `codegen:probe` is therefore absent on this path.
+
+Three details make the published ids and bytes match the previous plan:
+
+- The recorder starts from the probe's state: empty helper registries, fresh slot objects, and a cleared tally
+  (the contract prologue's sites are not part of the plan).
+- Recording takes the probe's skips, so its tallies and first-use allocation order match; the skipped bodies'
+  bytes are rebuilt in the finish phase.
+- Defined helpers are seeded live before the dead-DEFINE splice, because loop arms and shared checks are counted
+  under synthetic use keys.
+
+Framed compiles and single-body inlined direct shapes keep the existing non-materialising count and its
+content-keyed plan.
+
+## Byte-identical optimizations on the branch
+
+- Framed: compile the shipping rung once, with no discarded admission ladder or verifier-host build.
+- Direct: every body compiled once; the count comes from that emission (no probe walk).
+- Commitment uniqueness: allocation-free boundary scan; embed and verify in one pass per handler.
+- Artifact ASM: direct writer for opcodes and minimal pushes (55 → 5–7 ms per 624 KB conversion).
+- Verifier-binding assertion: scans the final script plus raw bodies; spans are ranges of that script.
+- Large `bytecodeToAsm` conversions are memoised by content (4 KB minimum, 8 entries).
+- Compact artifact bodies: bodies are offsets into `debug.bytecode`, resolved by one shipped resolver.
+
