+`codegen:probe` on the same runs: master 1,547–1,624 ms; branch 0 ms. The three samples are saved as
+`{SCRATCH}/final2/direct-<tree>-<n>.json` and `/framed-<tree>-<n>.json` with profile logs. All numbers above are from the clean build of the delivered code: the last source change was committed at 21:20
+(`7bd374aaf`), `solidc` was cleaned and rebuilt at 21:28 UTC on 2026-10-23, and commits after the build are
+docs/test only. Two machine checks hold on the delivered commit, both empty:
+
+    git diff --name-only 7bd374aaf..HEAD -- 'packages/*/src' 'packages/utils/src'
+    find packages/*/src -newer packages/solidc/dist/compiler.js
+
+Metadata is compared with the tree-parameterised `metadata-parity-marketplace.mjs`; the profile harness's
+`hashes.metadata` projection differs between the two trees because each tree runs its own harness version, so it
+is not used for cross-tree metadata comparison.
+
+## History
+
+The cache test fills the legacy usage-plan cache with 17 distinct single-function contracts (16 retained) and
+also asserts that multi-entry direct compiles leave it empty.
+
+Earlier rounds established that the probe's tallies and allocation order are load-bearing (bypassing the count
+produced a 5.38 MB script; counting the sites it skips changed the identity) and that a naive single pass cannot
+reproduce them. The implementation above resolves that by reproducing the probe's starting state and skips while
+recording, and by rebuilding the skipped bodies in the finish phase. The intermediate experiment remains on
+`defer-experiment` as history.
